            <ArticleTitle>[Surgical treatment of lumbar disk hernias in children and adolescents].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-5; discussion 25-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Results of examination and surgical treatment of 53 children and adolescents with lumbar disk herniation are presented. Examination revealed two types of neurological course of disease: the first type is observed in 75.5% of cases and is characterized by domination of radicular syndrome, and in the second type (24.5%) reflex syndrome is common. In children and adolescents with radicular type of course intralaminar approach was used, in reflex type--percutaneous nucleotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
